      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>And smeage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.1-3"/> man symle on æghwylce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.2-2"/> wisan, hu man fyrmest mæge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.3-2"/> ræd aredian þeode to þearfe ⁊ rihtne Cristendom swyðost aræran ⁊ æghwylce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.4"/> unlage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.5"/> geornost afyllan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ smeage man georne on æghwylce wísan, hu man fyrmæst mǽge rǽd aredian ðeode to ðearfe ⁊ rihtne Cristendóm swiðast arǽran ⁊ æghwylce unlage georne afyllen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>And smeaga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.1-4"/> man symle on æghwilce wisan, hu man fyrmest mege ræd aredian ðeode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.2-3"/> to þearfe ⁊ rihtne Cristendom swyðost áræron ⁊ æghwilce unlaga geornnod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.3-3"/> afyllan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Et perquiramus simul modis omnibus, quomodo precipuum possit consilium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.1-2"/> optineri ad profectum populi, rectaque Christianitas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.2"/> propensius erigi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.3"/>, quicquid iniustum est sollertius eneruari.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_11.lnote.oe.star"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Meditemur etiam semper omni modo, qualiter primum possimus concilium consulere genti ad utilitatem et rectam Christianitatem maxime exaltare omnemque iniusticiam deicere.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="11" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="178" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ smeage man georne<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_11.robnote.fn.10"/> on æghwylce wísan, hu man fyrmæst mǽge rǽd aredian ðeode to ðearfe ⁊ rihtne Cristendóm swiðast arǽran ⁊ æghwylce unlage geo<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IICn_11.robnote.fn.11"/>rne afyllen.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="258" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And smeage man symle on æghwylce wisan hu man fyrmest mæge ræd aredian þeode to þearfe and rihtne Cristendom swyðost aræran and æghwylce unlage geornost afyllan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>Und man sinne immer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_11.lnote.de.1"/> (eifrig <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) auf jede Weise, wie man zuvörderst dem Volke zum Nutzen einen vortheilhaften Plan ausfindig machen könne und rechtes Christenthum höchlichst aufrichten und jede Rechtswidrigkeit eifrigst (-ig <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) abschaffen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let people always (eagerly, B) consider in every way how they can first devise a beneficial plan for the good of the people, and most highly exalt true Christianity, and most (eagerly, B) abolish every abuse of law.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_11.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="179" ed="#robertson"/>And thought shall diligently be taken in every way how best to determine what is advisable for the public good, and how best to promote true Christianity and diligently suppress every injustice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="259" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And consideration must always be given in every way to how first to establish policy to meet the needs of the people and to best uphold the true Christian faith and to most zealously eradicate all injustice.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="316"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_40">VI Atr 40</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">VI Atr. 40</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_40">VI Atr 40–40.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 11-11:1: Cn 1018 24  VI Atr 40-40:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-061">Cn 1018 24</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 11-11:1: Cn 1018 24  VI Atr 40-40:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>used in I–II Cnut</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-061">Cn 1018 24</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 40, VI Æthelred 40.1 | D 24 | II Cnut 11, II Cnut 11.1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘geornnod’ is perhaps a slip for ‘geornost’. Liebermann compares VI Atr 40.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 317, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">symle: georne B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. I</hi> 6, 2<hi rend="italic">a</hi> healden <hi rend="italic">in A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. I 6, 2<hi rend="italic">a</hi> healden in A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o. c. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o. c. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tatis <hi rend="italic">KT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tatis KT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt T zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">11, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">11, 1 lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">smeaga <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">smeaga Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-wælce wysan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-wælce wysan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mæg <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mæg Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-wilce unlaga georne [<hi rend="italic">vgl. B</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-wilce unlaga georne [cf. B] Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> -ga <hi rend="italic">G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -ga G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später verbessert aus</hi> ðode</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later corrected from ðode</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">316</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Schreibfehler für</hi> geornost?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">slip for geornost?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_11.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu Q's <hi rend="italic">simul s. u</hi>. 84, 3; Af 34⁸</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On Q's <hi rend="italic">simul see below</hi> 84, 3; Af 34⁸</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_11.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the one following, cf. VI Atr. 40 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_11.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">178</biblScope></bibl><label>georne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">symle</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_11.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">178</biblScope></bibl><label>georne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geornost</hi> G, Ld; <hi rend="italic">-nnod</hi> A.</seg></note>
